8	10	1	processed\\pages\\1780472197296-GraphQL-1.png	GraphQL is a query language for APIs and a runtime for executing those queries against request .your data. It was developed by Facebook in 2012 and open-sourced in 2015. Unlike REST, which relies on multiple endpoints for different resources, GraphQL allows clients to request exactly the data they need in a single Endpoint. 🔹 Key Features of GraphQL: 1. Flexible Queries – Clients specify the structure of the response, reducing over- fetching and under-fetching of data. 2. Single Endpoint – Unlike REST APIs, which require multiple endpoints, GraphQL operates via a single endpoint (/graphql). 3. Strongly Typed Schema – The API is defined using a GraphQL schema , specifying data types and relationships. 4. Real-Time Updates – Supports subscriptions for real-time data updates. 5. Efficient and Faster – Reduces unnecessary network requests and payload size. 🔹 Example: 📌 GraphQL Query: query { user(id: 1) { name email posts { title content } } }	processed\\qrcodes\\1780472197296-GraphQL.docx-page-1-qr.png	f	native-pdf	\N	\N	2026-06-03 00:36:55.359522	09b1bdbca8e5a69fdb3fde2d0db707a3d9bfbff3e753471bd42340954b5a1bea	{"v": 1, "type": "page", "checksum": "demo-checksum", "documentId": "1780472197296-GraphQL.docx", "pageNumber": 1}
