89	20	1	processed\\pages\\1781684624228-DevOps (1)-1.png	DevOps 1⃣ What is DevOps ? DevOps is a culture, not a tool. It improves collaboration between Dev and Ops for faster and better software delivery. 2⃣ DevOps Foundation Principles – The Three Ways of DevOps 1. Flow 2. Feedback 3. Continual Learning 3⃣ First Way – FLOW Goal: Accelerate the flow of work from Development → Operations → Customers. Key Principles of Flow: • Understand the flow of work • Increase flow continuously • Never pass known defects downstream • Avoid local optimization that harms the whole system Example: Fix a bug before moving code to the next stage. 4⃣ Continuous Integration (CI) CI: Developers integrate code frequently with automated tests. 5⃣ Continuous Delivery Software is always ready to be released. Deployment is usually manual 📌 Example: You can deploy anytime, even if you don't deploy every change. 6⃣ Continuous Deployment	processed\\qrcodes\\1781684624228-DevOps (1).pdf-page-1-qr.png	f	native-pdf	\N	\N	2026-06-17 01:23:49.043201	5c6ea788bf70950ec541821a8e080741c9ba4e31da9af5e526106cb76b9dc3b8	{"v": 1, "type": "page", "checksum": "demo-checksum", "documentId": "1781684624228-DevOps (1).pdf", "pageNumber": 1}
90	20	2	processed\\pages\\1781684624228-DevOps (1)-2.png	Every change that passes tests is deployed automatically. Difference from Continuous Delivery: • Delivery → Manual deploy • Deployment → Automatic deploy Note: Not suitable for all companies (regulations). Release vs Deployment • Deployment: Install software • Release: Make features visible to users Example: Code is deployed but feature is hidden. First Way in Action • Visualize work using Kanban (JIRA) • Limit Work In Progress (WIP) • Use automation tools Second Way – FEEDBACK Goal: Fast feedback to detect problems early. Improvement Kata (Very Important) 1. Vision 2. Current condition 3. Target condition 4. Small experiments Example: Pull request + peer review before merge. Third Way – Continual Learning & Experimentation Learn from failure and success.	processed\\qrcodes\\1781684624228-DevOps (1).pdf-page-2-qr.png	f	native-pdf	\N	\N	2026-06-17 01:23:49.053393	358754daa6ae0698f70a215ebd54b2590958b2eec7b7281af63b58e0a5f460a8	{"v": 1, "type": "page", "checksum": "demo-checksum", "documentId": "1781684624228-DevOps (1).pdf", "pageNumber": 2}
91	20	3	processed\\pages\\1781684624228-DevOps (1)-3.png	Learn from failure and success. Encourage experiments and practice. DevOps Lifecycle Plan → Code → Build → Test → Release → Deploy → Monitor DevOps Tools The file mentions tools in general Used for CI, CD, monitoring, automation.	processed\\qrcodes\\1781684624228-DevOps (1).pdf-page-3-qr.png	f	native-pdf	\N	\N	2026-06-17 01:23:49.055235	adfb2077f79e604ea3bfa7c61cc31563b627b9d99301530007cac50407bd4e1f	{"v": 1, "type": "page", "checksum": "demo-checksum", "documentId": "1781684624228-DevOps (1).pdf", "pageNumber": 3}
