101	26	2	processed\\pages\\1782324055497-Kanban Framework-02.png	3 Origins and Evolution Kanban is a Japanese word that literally means " visual card ". Kanban cards were originally used in Toyota to limit the amount of inventory tied up in " work in progress " on a manufacturing floor. Kanban not only reduces excess inventory waste, but also the time spent in producing it. The original author of Kanban was Taiichi Ohno . Kanban has been used in Lean Production (Lean Thinking) KANBAN was formalized in 2010 by David Anderson	processed\\qrcodes\\1782324055497-Kanban Framework.pdf-page-2-qr.png	f	native-pdf	\N	\N	2026-06-24 11:01:12.123189	6f7c685be002c1ed282cfb5c6d92d530c483722986701a95c50ba427e16f3162	{"v": 1, "type": "page", "checksum": "demo-checksum", "documentId": "1782324055497-Kanban Framework.pdf", "pageNumber": 2}
