161	35	1	processed\\pages\\1782553576113-back-end+login-01.png	Web Services Implement JWT authentication in a Spring Boot application	processed\\qrcodes\\1782553576113-back-end+login.pdf-page-1-qr.png	f	native-pdf	\N	\N	2026-06-27 02:46:49.376959	d43421b2ef3c318c612aeddd981ffec37c7a51dbbb6c441efbab7bcfa2daec51	{"v": 1, "type": "page", "checksum": "demo-checksum", "documentId": "1782553576113-back-end+login.pdf", "pageNumber": 1}
162	35	2	processed\\pages\\1782553576113-back-end+login-02.png	Introduction One of the most popular and effective authentication methods in modern web applications is JSON Web Tokens (JWT). It provides a flexible and stateless way to verify users' identities and secure API endpoints; it is also called Token-Based Authentication.	processed\\qrcodes\\1782553576113-back-end+login.pdf-page-2-qr.png	f	native-pdf	\N	\N	2026-06-27 02:46:50.200527	d70601aa6a4725667ae63f33d5d22e1fed2164d6b38c28cbaf8c65df8a8d7f10	{"v": 1, "type": "page", "checksum": "demo-checksum", "documentId": "1782553576113-back-end+login.pdf", "pageNumber": 2}
163	35	3	processed\\pages\\1782553576113-back-end+login-03.png	Overview of API Endpoints This API provides both public and protected routes. The authentication system ensures secure access: - Public Routes: /auth/signup → Allows users to register. /auth/login → AuthenƟcates users and provides access tokens. - Protected Routes (Require Authentication): /users/me → Retrieves the currently authenƟcated user. /users → Retrieves a list of authenƟcated users. /products/** Public routes are accessible to everyone, while protected routes require a valid authentication token.	processed\\qrcodes\\1782553576113-back-end+login.pdf-page-3-qr.png	f	native-pdf	\N	\N	2026-06-27 02:46:51.014228	ebba15be5b0f02b5dd82aed71fef0fcd20f35c85ae0145af3f4e6062c2211d76	{"v": 1, "type": "page", "checksum": "demo-checksum", "documentId": "1782553576113-back-end+login.pdf", "pageNumber": 3}
164	35	4	processed\\pages\\1782553576113-back-end+login-04.png	Prerequisites Before starting, ensure you have the following installed Ჰ JDK 17 or higher – Required to run the application. ᳀ IntelliJ IDEA – Recommended IDE for development. ᲼ PostgreSQL – Database for storing user data. Შ HTTP Client (Postman) – To test API endpoints. Make sure all dependencies are properly configured before proceeding Note: Use Spring Initializr to simplify project creation and configuration.	processed\\qrcodes\\1782553576113-back-end+login.pdf-page-4-qr.png	f	native-pdf	\N	\N	2026-06-27 02:46:51.821138	4236e7b9cbc2fcc0a06e799f7eceaa43081fa0ad2c2aaab529b8fcf594768918	{"v": 1, "type": "page", "checksum": "demo-checksum", "documentId": "1782553576113-back-end+login.pdf", "pageNumber": 4}
166	35	6	processed\\pages\\1782553576113-back-end+login-06.png	Configure the database connection spring.application.name=jwt-auth-api # Server Configuration server.port=8081 # PostgreSQL Database Configuration spring.datasource.url=jdbc:postgresql://localhost:5432/users_db spring.datasource.driverClassName=org.postgresql.Driver spring.datasource.username=postgres spring.datasource.password=0000 # Hibernate (JPA) Settings spring.jpa.hibernate.ddl-auto=update spring.jpa.open-in-view=false spring.jpa.properties.hibernate.dialect=org.hibernate.dialect.PostgreSQLDialect spring.jpa.show-sql=true spring.jpa.properties.hibernate.format_sql=true	processed\\qrcodes\\1782553576113-back-end+login.pdf-page-6-qr.png	f	native-pdf	\N	\N	2026-06-27 02:46:53.449682	9b3d8b6c94097b2656c71e85009195ea495ae969f66f2ffeac8282e460911e92	{"v": 1, "type": "page", "checksum": "demo-checksum", "documentId": "1782553576113-back-end+login.pdf", "pageNumber": 6}
167	35	7	processed\\pages\\1782553576113-back-end+login-07.png	Install JSON Web Token dependencies <dependencies> <dependency> <groupId>io.jsonwebtoken</groupId> <artifactId>jjwt-api</artifactId> <version>0.11.5</version> </dependency> <dependency> <groupId>io.jsonwebtoken</groupId> <artifactId>jjwt-impl</artifactId> <version>0.11.5</version> </dependency> <dependency> <groupId>io.jsonwebtoken</groupId> <artifactId>jjwt-jackson</artifactId> <version>0.11.5</version> </dependency> </dependencies>	processed\\qrcodes\\1782553576113-back-end+login.pdf-page-7-qr.png	f	native-pdf	\N	\N	2026-06-27 02:46:54.261951	422306e9be1d05a0149d817f12d1b3403703dc874bad7fe1e65ebb6752dcf8ea	{"v": 1, "type": "page", "checksum": "demo-checksum", "documentId": "1782553576113-back-end+login.pdf", "pageNumber": 7}
