186	35	26	processed\\pages\\1782553576113-back-end+login-26.png	Conclusion Wrap up In this App, we saw how to implement the JSON Web Token authentication in a Spring Boot application. Here are the main steps of this process: 1. A JWT authentication filter extracts and validates the token from the request header. 2. Whitelist some API routes and protect those requiring a token. 3. Perform the authentication, generate the JWT, and set an expiration time. 4. Use the JWT generated to access protected routes. 5. Catch authentication exceptions to customize the response sent to the client.	processed\\qrcodes\\1782553576113-back-end+login.pdf-page-26-qr.png	f	native-pdf	\N	\N	2026-06-27 02:47:09.662607	5b2d1e389699277211262a96fa85b31e05c6236420754030c0c3e61dcec488c8	{"v": 1, "type": "page", "checksum": "demo-checksum", "documentId": "1782553576113-back-end+login.pdf", "pageNumber": 26}
