278	52	6	processed\\pages\\1782740166555-FinalAiReportTP1 (1)-06.png	 sign(...) applies the **sign function**, which is the perceptron's activation function: ӯ i = sign ( X i ∗ W ) = { + 1 if X i ∗ W ≥ 0 − 1 if X i ∗ W < 0 2. Compute the error: (sign(X(ind(i),:)*W)-yi(ind(i)))  yi(ind(i)) is the actual label y i  sign(X(ind(i),:)*W) is the predicted label ӯ i  The difference : e = ӯ i − y i  This measures the classification error:  If the prediction is correct  ӯ i =y i , then e=0  No weight update.  If misclassified  ӯ i ≠ y i : ӯ i =+ 1 but y i = -1  then e=2 (overestimation) ӯ i = − 1 but y i = +1  then e= -2 (underestimation) 3. Compute the Direction of Weight Update: Dir=(sign(X(ind(i),:)*W)-yi(ind(i)))*X(ind(i),:)  Multiplies the error e by the feature vector X i  The vector points in the direction of the correction needed:  If the prediction was too high ( ӯ i > y i ), Dir will be positive, decreasing the weight values.  If the prediction was too low ( ӯ i < y i ), Dir will be negative, increasing the weight values.  Syntax Explanation of updating the weight vector: W=W-pas*Dir'  η (pas = 0.1) is the learning rate, which controls how much we adjust the weights. W = W −η × Dir  Since Dir is a row vector, we transpose (Dir') to match the dimension of `W` (column vector).  Dir determines how much and in which direction the weight vector should be adjusted.  The perceptron rule ensures that the weight update pushes the decision boundary in a way that moves the misclassified sample toward the correct side.  If the sample is correctly classified, Dir becomes zero, and no update happens.  Equivalent Perceptron Code Syntax in Python Programing Language:	processed\\qrcodes\\1782740166555-FinalAiReportTP1 (1).pdf-page-6-qr.png	f	native-pdf	\N	\N	2026-06-29 06:36:47.80113	a1426818c4b2057ed1e24395c263124931e6c8dc60a1c04b9ce647524d155d1b	{"v": 1, "type": "page", "checksum": "demo-checksum", "documentId": "1782740166555-FinalAiReportTP1 (1).pdf", "pa