284	52	12	processed\\pages\\1782740166555-FinalAiReportTP1 (1)-12.png	def perceptron(X, yi, learning_rate=0.1, max_iterations=50): """ Perceptron Learning Algorithm in Python. Parameters: X : numpy array of shape (m, n) - Training data yi : numpy array of shape (m, 1) - Labels (+1 or -1) learning_rate : float - Step size for weight updates max_iterations : int - Maximum number of iterations Returns: west : numpy array - Weight vector excluding bias best : float - Bias term cout : int - Number of misclassified samples after training """ # Initialize weight vector randomly W = np.random.randn(X.shape[1], 1) # random weights vector k = 0 # Iteration counter cout = np.sum(np.abs(np.sign(np.dot(X, W)) - yi)) # Count misclassified samples while cout > 0 and k < max_iterations: k += 1 # Increment iteration count indices = np.random.permutation( len (X)) # Shuffle data indices to avoid biases	processed\\qrcodes\\1782740166555-FinalAiReportTP1 (1).pdf-page-12-qr.png	f	native-pdf	\N	\N	2026-06-29 06:36:52.715713	af7cdaedcbf242e44742db79f904d00d396b3292bb96cb752e40482b3d4be82b	{"v": 1, "type": "page", "checksum": "demo-checksum", "documentId": "1782740166555-FinalAiReportTP1 (1).pdf", "pageNumber": 12}
