288	52	16	processed\\pages\\1782740166555-FinalAiReportTP1 (1)-16.png	The above simulation shows how efficient the hard limit transfer function at classifying this problem.  To experiment even more, we decided to implement a perceptron function that utilizes "sigmoid" as the transfer function. Our aim is to test how a probabilistic classification could differ in solving such a problem. import torch import torch.nn as nn import torch.optim as optim # Define input (features) and target (labels) P = torch.tensor([[1, 2, 0.1, 2, 0.2, 3, 0.1, 1.5, 0.5, 1.6], [0.1, 0.2, 0.3, 0.3, 0.4, 0.4, 0.5, 0.5, 0.6, 0.7]], dtype=torch.float32) T = torch.tensor([1, 1, 0, 1, 0, 1, 0, 1, 0, 0], dtype=torch.float32).view(-1, 1) # Reshape for PyTorch	processed\\qrcodes\\1782740166555-FinalAiReportTP1 (1).pdf-page-16-qr.png	f	native-pdf	\N	\N	2026-06-29 06:36:55.961648	ba9305d2809550531c5c8bd017f57199e1b25c587bc7aaf1de09e70b64de99ca	{"v": 1, "type": "page", "checksum": "demo-checksum", "documentId": "1782740166555-FinalAiReportTP1 (1).pdf", "pageNumber": 16}
289	52	17	processed\\pages\\1782740166555-FinalAiReportTP1 (1)-17.png	# Define a simple perceptron model class Perceptron(nn.Module): def __init__( self ): super (Perceptron, self ).__init__() self .fc = nn.Linear(2, 1) # 2 input features, 1 output def forward( self , x): return torch.sigmoid( self .fc(x)) # Using sigmoid activation # Initialize model, loss function, and optimizer model = Perceptron() criterion = nn.BCELoss() # Binary Cross-Entropy for classification optimizer = optim.SGD(model.parameters(), lr=0.1) # Stochastic Gradient Descent # Train the model epochs = 50 for epoch in range (epochs): optimizer.zero_grad() # Clear previous gradients output = model(P.T) # Forward pass loss = criterion(output, T) # Compute loss loss.backward() # Backpropagation optimizer.step() # Update weights if epoch % 10 == 0: print (f"Epoch {epoch+1}/{epochs}, Loss: {loss.item():.4f}") # Test the trained model with torch.no_grad():	processed\\qrcodes\\1782740166555-FinalAiReportTP1 (1).pdf-page-17-qr.png	f	native-pdf	\N	\N	2026-06-29 06:36:56.771328	27551b6b8b23a2401fbbedc9846f56f196ec521679093f5574467a2a51488ec7	{"v": 1, "type": "page", "checksum": "demo-checksum", "documentId": "1782740166555-FinalAiReportTP1 (1).pdf", "pageNumber": 17}
