301	52	29	processed\\pages\\1782740166555-FinalAiReportTP1 (1)-29.png	Conclusion During the research done for this report, we implemented multiple types of perceptron based neural networks for data classification. We started off by implementing a network that could classify some basic datasets via binary classification, but a one that fails at classifying more complex datasets that require special handling. Then we implemented yet another network similar to the first one, but this time using some built-in matlab tools, as well as experimented with Pytorch library and some probabilistic classification methods. In the end we built a simple multi-layer neural network, and again we used Pytorch to experiment with the concepts. Our results proved that different tools will achieve similar results in nature, but one is more complex than the other. Pytorch, while being an industry standard, it seems like an overkill for the simple datasets we are working with and thus why the output of the Matlab programs was much more accurate.	processed\\qrcodes\\1782740166555-FinalAiReportTP1 (1).pdf-page-29-qr.png	f	native-pdf	\N	\N	2026-06-29 06:37:06.55019	701342c43c35fea97b00466c0e6aad63adec93314bbfe62ffa07d8dda5b28dde	{"v": 1, "type": "page", "checksum": "demo-checksum", "documentId": "1782740166555-FinalAiReportTP1 (1).pdf", "pageNumber": 29}
