68	67	origins, evolution, kanban, japanese, word, that, literally, means, visual, card, kanban, cards, were, originally, used, toyota, limit, amount, inventory, tied, work, progress, manufacturing, floor., kanban, only, reduces, excess, inventory, waste,, also, time, spent, producing, original, author, kanban, taiichi, ohno, kanban, been, used, lean, production, (lean, thinking), kanban, formalized, 2010, david	3 Origins and Evolution Kanban is a Japanese word that literally means " visual card ". Kanban cards were originally used in Toyota to limit the amount of inventory tied up in " work in progress " on a manufacturing floor. Kanban not only reduces excess inventory waste, but also the time spent in producing it. The original author of Kanban was Taiichi Ohno . Kanban has been used in Lean Production (Lean Thinking) KANBAN was formalized in 2010 by David Anderson	xenova-minilm-68	2026-06-24 09:09:30.000231	[-0.031825244426727295, -0.07678826153278351, -0.062209196388721466, -0.017931940034031868, 0.0005684986826963723, -0.023874850943684578, 0.010370573028922081, -0.0013998978538438678, 0.06379088014364243, -0.06701485812664032, 0.07497673481702805, 0.004597931168973446, -0.04908635839819908, -0.004623635206371546, 0.015331445261836052, -0.0637534037232399, 0.012121275067329407, 0.04197349771857262, 0.04548869654536247, -0.021790524944663048, 0.056705959141254425, 0.015768595039844513, 0.03583432734012604, 0.05673188716173172, 0.048702679574489594, 0.033996861428022385, -0.01135693583637476, -0.02659597061574459, 0.0845852643251419, -0.03786905109882355, -0.020384646952152252, 0.06780902296304703, 0.10939426720142365, 0.022977430373430252, -0.008246473036706448, -0.011566489934921265, -0.03665951266884804, 0.0396755151450634, -0.033489666879177094, -0.05342050641775131, -0.08317632228136063, -0.006355422083288431, -0.024343978613615036, 0.01343566831201315, 0.07205663621425629, -0.0023223566822707653, -0.0034189235884696245, -0.021600261330604553, -0.05030354857