69	69	kanban, concept, cores, visualize, visualize, workflow, split, entire, work, into, defined, sections, states,, visualized, named, columns, wall., write, each, item, card, column, indicate, where, item, workflow., limit, limit, assign, explicit, limits, many, items, progress, each, workflow, section, state., i.e.,, work, progress, (wip), limited, each, workflow, state., measure, measure, lead, time	5 Kanban Concept Cores Visualize Visualize Workflow • Split the entire work into defined sections or states, visualized as named columns on a wall. • Write each item on a card and put in a column to indicate where the item is in the workflow. Limit Limit WIP • Assign explicit limits to how many items can be in progress at each workflow section / state. • i.e., Work in Progress (WIP) is limited in each workflow state. Measure Measure the Lead Time • Lead Time, also known as cycle time, is the average time to complete one item. • Measure the Lead Time and optimize the process to make the Lead Time as small and predictable as possible. Direct implementation of a Lean Pull Scheduling System . An item can move to the next segment / state only when it obtains a slot in there.	xenova-minilm-69	2026-06-24 09:09:30.004056	[-0.008575629442930222, -0.0057561323046684265, -0.01366033498197794, -0.025333356112241745, -0.022451382130384445, -0.03565184772014618, -0.041814353317022324, 0.056855980306863785, -0.03612744063138962, 0.009459351189434528, 0.010238133370876312, -0.017363905906677246, -0.08085528761148453, -0.02407694421708584, 0.001148231327533722, -0.013329521752893925, 0.05710892006754875, -0.015333486720919609, -0.016135042533278465, -0.12771353125572205, 0.07007574290037155, -0.027460811659693718, -0.02383613958954811, 0.02970280312001705, -0.0155892139300704, 0.006109710782766342, -0.06243613362312317, -0.007599319331347942, -0.009298962540924549, -0.02619532123208046, -0.03048367239534855, -0.06235197186470032, 0.07315899431705475, 0.054883670061826706, -0.03961682