102	133	devops, what, devops, devops, culture,, tool., improves, collaboration, between, faster, better, software, delivery., devops, foundation, principles, three, ways, devops, flow, feedback, continual, learning, first, flow, goal:, accelerate, flow, work, from, development, operations, customers., principles, flow:, understand, flow, work, increase, flow, continuously, never, pass, known, defects, downstream, avoid, local, optimization, that	DevOps 1⃣ What is DevOps ? DevOps is a culture, not a tool. It improves collaboration between Dev and Ops for faster and better software delivery. 2⃣ DevOps Foundation Principles – The Three Ways of DevOps 1. Flow 2. Feedback 3. Continual Learning 3⃣ First Way – FLOW Goal: Accelerate the flow of work from Development → Operations → Customers. Key Principles of Flow: • Understand the flow of work • Increase flow continuously • Never pass known defects downstream • Avoid local optimization that harms the whole system Example: Fix a bug before moving code to the next stage. 4⃣ Continuous Integration (CI) CI: Developers integrate code frequently with automated tests. 5⃣ Continuous Delivery Software is always ready to be released. Deployment is usually manual 📌 Example: You can deploy anytime, even if you don't deploy every change. 6⃣ Continuous Deployment	xenova-minilm-102	2026-06-24 13:36:37.703166	[0.04654114320874214, -0.00605468126013875, 0.02523271180689335, -0.02351011149585247, -0.006957056932151318, -0.061948731541633606, -0.02594483457505703, -0.0166886318475008, 0.039256393909454346, 0.043076176196336746, -0.0006720208912156522, 0.012796369381248951, -0.002596887294203043, -0.023640131577849388, 0.003357592737302184, -0.03274794667959213, -0.021371284499764442, 0.005013305228203535, -0.01686067506670952, -0.054977986961603165, -0.013707323931157589, -0.010054530575871468, -0.016358407214283943, 0.057990506291389465, -0.04004288837313652, 0.04136982560157776, -0.005997989792376757, 0.005185883957892656, 0.02799160778522