104	136	togaf, chapter, introduction, togaf, chapter, introduction, togaf, what, togaf, togaf, (the, open, group, architecture, framework), enterprise, architecture, framework., helps, organizations, design,, develop,, use,, maintain, enterprise, architectures, using, best, practices, iterative, method., purpose, togaf, togaf, provides, standard, method, align, systems, with, business, goals., definition, architecture, togaf), architecture, means:, formal, description, system.	Togaf Chapter 1: Introduction to TOGAF ### Chapter 1: Introduction to TOGAF 1. What is TOGAF ? TOGAF (The Open Group Architecture Framework) is an enterprise architecture framework. It helps organizations design, develop, use, and maintain enterprise architectures using best practices and an iterative method. --- 2. Purpose of TOGAF TOGAF provides a standard method to align IT systems with business goals. --- 3. Definition of Architecture (in TOGAF) Architecture means: 1. A formal description of a system. 2. The structure of components, their relationships, and the rules governing their evolution. --- 4. Types of Architecture in TOGAF (Important) TOGAF covers four types of architecture: - Business Architecture: business strategy, processes, and governance. - Data Architecture: structure and management of data. - Application Architecture: applications and their interactions. - Technology Architecture: hardware, software, and networks.	xenova-minilm-104	2026-06-24 13:57:31.007441	[0.005253309849649668, -0.028716349974274635, -0.08789686858654022, -0.02364717237651348, 0.008539692498743534, -0.004304372239857912, 0.026487059891223907, -0.02571278065443039, 0.00788308959454298, -0.019256437197327614, -0.08585529029369354, -0.011079268530011177, -0.013006594963371754, -0.012712480500340462, 0.008866352960467339, -0.09615282714366913, 0.03197364881634712, -0.04495808482170105, -0.02626369148492813, -0.05499416962265968, -0.0475577674806118, 0.016984930261969566, -0.03638436645269394, 0.0022317061666