188	219	kanban, characteristics, pull, approach, importance, this, approach, consists, resolving, friction, between, teams., i.e.,, teams, collaborate, while, first, performing, better, than, second, one,, likely, that, pushes, more, work, than, other, handle., pull, approach,, next, team, pulls, work, only, when, ready, pull, approach, implemented, adding, buffer, with, limited, capacity, between, teams., benefits	11 Kanban Characteristics Pull Approach • The importance of this approach consists in resolving friction between teams. – i.e., two teams collaborate while the first one is performing better than the second one, – it is likely that it pushes more work than the other can handle. – In Pull Approach, the next team pulls work only when it is ready for it. • Pull Approach is implemented by adding a buffer with limited capacity between the two teams. • The benefits of Pull Approach are: – Avoids piling-up of work. – Reduces wait time. – Facilitates a team to maintain constant pace and focus on quality. – Provides resource balancing.	xenova-minilm-188	2026-06-29 04:19:22.295346	[0.012066845782101154, -0.03529718890786171, -0.009832019917666912, -0.03462866321206093, -0.015220167115330696, 0.026963215321302414, -0.03857196494936943, 0.04969758167862892, 0.053780458867549896, 0.0038347390946000814, 0.05887933075428009, -0.01687365397810936, -0.05331426486372948, 0.01209656149148941, 0.09780068695545197, -0.03669130057096481, 0.053633902221918106, -0.006769149098545313, -0.022288905456662178, -0.05660563334822655, 0.022979341447353363, -0.05998389795422554, -0.05213125795125961, 0.006718778517097235, -0.04901870712637901, -0.05179762467741966, -0.07267419248819351, 0.03102153167128563, 0.003887530881911516, -0.08138099312782288, -0.06436564773321152, -0.02136523835361004, -0.021754229441285133, 0.03617655858397484, -0.08356683701276779, 0.03450899198651314, -0.04735766723752022, 0.07543713599443436, -0.030448665842413902, 0.0191339198499918, -0.07251930981874466, -