284	314	kanban, characteristics, continuous, delivery, benefits, continuous, delivery, are:, short, release, cycles, result, continuous, delivery, growing, product, regular, interval., continuous, interactions, with, customer., understand, what, customer, wants., produce, what, customer, needs., feedback, delivered, modules., limited, requirements, each, release, cycle., developers, overloaded, with, requests., this, enables, them, focus, delivery., there, partially, completed	14 Kanban Characteristics Continuous Delivery Benefits of continuous delivery are: • Short release cycles result in continuous delivery of growing product at regular interval. • Continuous interactions with the customer. • To understand what customer wants. • Produce what the customer needs. • Feedback on delivered modules. • Limited requirements in each release cycle. • Developers are not overloaded with requests. This enables them to focus on the delivery. • There is no partially completed work. • Focus is on finishing work than on starting work. • This enables focus on sustaining pace and quality of the product. • Deliver before the customer changes mind. • Optimize flow of Work from beginning to end. • Helps in incremental process improvements.	xenova-minilm-284	2026-07-06 03:39:01.486498	[0.029382867738604546, -0.028919164091348648, 0.0298409815877676, -0.02449874021112919, -0.012034500949084759, 0.0236926581710577, -0.003401966765522957, 0.0556454099714756, -0.013010638765990734, -0.009124630130827427, 0.0731252133846283, 0.04524676501750946, -0.03980600833892822, 0.021035943180322647, 0.05564815551042557, -0.01784818433225155, 0.06966300308704376, -0.04866355285048485, -0.042070336639881134, -0.0627310574054718, -0.010861271061003208, 0.02113567851483822, -0.03456203639507294, 0.07491326332092285, -0.07037820667028427, -0.005567382089793682, -0.0726175308227539, -0.038253434002399445, 0.02851693145930767, -0.07948319613933563, 0.006067924667149782, 0.029751215130090714, 0.02998722717165