293	325	graphql, query, language, apis, runtime, executing, those, queries, against, request, .your, data., developed, facebook, 2012, open-sourced, 2015., unlike, rest,, which, relies, multiple, endpoints, different, resources,, graphql, allows, clients, request, exactly, data, they, need, single, endpoint., features, graphql:, flexible, queries, clients, specify, structure, response,, reducing, over-, fetching, under-fetching, data., single, endpoint	GraphQL is a query language for APIs and a runtime for executing those queries against request .your data. It was developed by Facebook in 2012 and open-sourced in 2015. Unlike REST, which relies on multiple endpoints for different resources, GraphQL allows clients to request exactly the data they need in a single Endpoint. 🔹 Key Features of GraphQL: 1. Flexible Queries – Clients specify the structure of the response, reducing over- fetching and under-fetching of data. 2. Single Endpoint – Unlike REST APIs, which require multiple endpoints, GraphQL operates via a single endpoint (/graphql). 3. Strongly Typed Schema – The API is defined using a GraphQL schema , specifying data types and relationships. 4. Real-Time Updates – Supports subscriptions for real-time data updates. 5. Efficient and Faster – Reduces unnecessary network requests and payload size. 🔹 Example: 📌 GraphQL Query: query { user(id: 1) { name email posts { title content } } }	xenova-minilm-293	2026-08-05 07:48:31.570323	[-0.046281278133392334, 0.048926301300525665, -0.005552274640649557, 0.060029253363609314, -0.06546451896429062, -0.02860819362103939, -0.06886300444602966, 0.009159639477729797, 0.009591294452548027, 0.04047231003642082, -0.03546442836523056, -0.009263478219509125, 0.060461971908807755, 0.012077736668288708, 0.08347279578447342, 0.04664451628923416, 0.06714681535959244, -0.08915779739618301, -0.008566081523895264, -0.013247786089777946, 0.014589931815862656, -0.007089183200150728, 0.004999162163585424, 0.015150940045714378, 0.04487760737